    max_reachable = 0
    for i in range(len(obstacles)):
        if i > max_reachable:
            return False  # Player cannot move forward
        max_reachable = max(max_reachable, i + obstacles[i])
        if max_reachable >= len(obstacles) - 1:
            return True  # Player can reach the last position
    return False  # Player cannot reach the last position
```
The `navigate_obstacles` function iterates through the list of obstacles, updating the maximum reachable position based on the current position and obstacle value. If at any point the player cannot move forward (`i > max_reachable`), the function returns `False`. If the player can reach the last position, the function returns `True`. If the loop completes without reaching the last position, the function returns `False`.

